6. Advantages of APIs

Enable communication between applications.

Support integration with third-party services.

Encourage code reuse.

Separate frontend and backend responsibilities.

Help applications exchange data.

7. Interview Questions

Q1. What is an API?

An API is an interface that allows different software applications to communicate.

Q2. What is an API endpoint?

An endpoint is a URL or route used to access a resource or perform an operation.

Q3. What is JSON?

JSON stands for JavaScript Object Notation. It is a lightweight data-exchange format.

Q4. What is an HTTP request?

An HTTP request is a message sent by a client to a server to retrieve or modify information.

Q5. What is a REST API?

A REST API is an API designed around REST architectural principles, commonly using HTTP methods to work with resources.

